Description: VA-API video decode driver for Rockchip RK3588 (MPP)
 Hardware video decode on the RK3588/RK3588S video decoders through
 Rockchip MPP, offered to applications through VA-API (libva): H.264,
 HEVC, VP8, VP9 and AV1, 8- and 10-bit, with DRM PRIME surface export
 (NV12 and P010). Clients that export each decoded surface (Firefox, mpv)
 get 8-bit pictures straight from MPP's buffers without a copy. The 10-bit
 conversion runs on the RGA 2D engine. AV1 pictures a client syncs early
 are decoded once only with an MPP that has the deferred reference refresh
 (librockchip-mpp1 +pd32 or later, RK3588); with other MPP builds they are
 decoded twice.
 Needs a Rockchip BSP kernel that provides /dev/mpp_service.
 .
 Also installs panthor_drv_video.so and panfrost_drv_video.so links so
 libva finds the driver on Panthor/Panfrost GPU stacks. Replaces the
 earlier rockchip-vaapi-driver package.
